    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a memory-mapped hardware register. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class is a zero-overhead wrapper around a specific memory address. It enforces access policies (Read-Only, Write-Only, Read-Write) and data width constraints at compile time using C++20 concepts.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Addr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The physical base address of the register. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
